# Topic

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Topic.py`

An organizational category that groups related events and tasks. Topics form a
directed acyclic graph (DAG) via `parent_ids`. Tag and layout inheritance from
parents is resolved by `backending`, not here.

---

## YAML form accepted

```yaml
topics:
  - id: math
    name: Mathematics
    description: "All math-related events and tasks"
    tags: [school, academic]
    parent_ids: [studies]
    layout:
      background:
        type: solid
        color: "#3498db"
```

---

## Fields

| Field         | Type                    | Required | Description                                          |
|---------------|-------------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------------|
| `id`          | `str`                   | yes      | Unique identifier used to reference this topic       |
| `name`        | `str`                   | yes      | Human-readable display name                          |
| `description` | `str \| None`           | no       | Optional longer description                          |
| `tags`        | `list[str]`             | no       | Empty list if omitted; inherited by child topics and tasks |
| `parent_ids`  | `list[str]`             | no       | IDs of parent topics; empty list if omitted          |
| `layout`      | `Layout \| str \| None` | no       | Inline layout or reference to a named layout id      |

---

## Interface

```
Topic
  + id: str
  + name: str
  + description: str | None
  + tags: list[str]
  + parent_ids: list[str]
  + layout: Layout | str | None
```

---

## Notes

- Frozen dataclass.
- `id` uniqueness across all topics in a configuration is enforced by
  `backending`, not here.
- `parent_ids` stores raw string references; the DAG is assembled by
  `backending`. Cycles are detected there too.
- `layout` typed as `Layout | str | None`:
  - `str` — unresolved reference to a named layout id.
  - `Layout` — inline definition.
  - `None` — no layout for this topic.
- `tags` defaults to `[]` (not `None`) so callers can safely iterate without
  a `None`-check.
